meta {
  name: 22 Send (Internal Transfer)
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/{{sampleId}}/send
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "destinationBranchId": "{{branchId}}",
    "sendDate": "2026-07-20T10:00:00.000Z",
    "sendTime": "10:00",
    "sampleForm": "Whole blood, 1 tube",
    "logisticsType": "Lab Vehicle",
    "logisticsPerson": "Amit Driver",
    "notes": "Sent to processing branch"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data[0]) bru.setEnvVar("transferId", data[0].id);
}

tests {
  test("transition applied (or rejected by the state machine)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 422]);
  });
}

docs {
  Send (Internal Transfer) — **Accepted → Sent (Internal)**, creating an INTERNAL
  `SampleTransfer` at `IN_TRANSIT`. `destinationBranchId` is another branch in the
  same tenant (validated); omit it to assign later via **Assign Center** (§A.7).
  Captures `transferId`. Bulk: `POST /accession/order-samples/bulk/send` with `ids[]`.

  ## Group override (bulk) — `force` / `skipInvalid`

  The bulk variant accepts the same group flags as the sample actions. `force:
  true` (grouped in-house Actions dropdown) creates the transfer for **every** id
  regardless of its current status, forcing each sample to `SENT_INTERNAL` with no
  §A.9 legality check. `skipInvalid: true` instead skips ids not in a legal
  (Accepted) state rather than failing the batch. Same flags apply to
  `bulk/forward` and `bulk/outsource`.

  **The destination must OFFER every test on the tube (Phase 1).** A tube can only go to a branch that has an
  ACTIVE Lab Test List entry for each of its tests. The match goes through the tenant test both branches copied
  (the sender's Branch Master Data test -> `sourceMasterLabTestId` -> the destination's Branch Master Data test
  with the same tenant test -> an active, not deleted list entry); any of the destination's lists counts. A test
  with no tenant link (hand-created at the branch) cannot be matched and counts as NOT offered. A free-text tube
  test (no catalogue test) is skipped. Otherwise: 422 `DESTINATION_LACKS_TEST`, "<Branch> does not offer: <tests>.
  Choose another branch." (at most five test names, then "and N more"); nothing is changed.
  Where it applies: here (only when a `destinationBranchId` is given - Send without a destination stays allowed and
  is checked when the centre is assigned), Assign / Edit Center, `apply-center-changes` and Accept. In a group send
  with `skipInvalid` the tube is skipped with this reason and code; a strict group send is refused as a whole.
  Forward / Outsource are not affected. `GET /branches/options?forSampleIds=` tells the picker which branches
  qualify.
}
